[11:04] I built and saved the phone agent. The brief has no practice customers (`public-test-set.json` is empty), so I ran no customer tests. The only tests were the workflow check, which found 0 errors and 0 warnings, and a local run of both code steps on sample data.
[11:04] 
[11:04] **How I read the memos:**
[11:04] - **OM-3 (3 February)** comes before the 2 March policy extract, so the extract replaces it. Its 20:00 callback limit and its car-loan rule are not used.
[11:04] - **OM-17 (9 October)** applies. Callbacks are booked from 09:00 to 17:00. The deadline for customers 8 to 45 days late is the 6th business day; the early band keeps the 12th.
[11:04] 
[11:04] **How the call is built:**
[11:04] - **Order of steps:** opening, then the identity check, then the account lookup, then the payment conversation. A separate step handles someone else answering and booking a callback.
[11:04] - **Exits and endings:** separate steps handle hardship and the three transfer queues. There are 18 endings, each with a fixed goodbye.
[11:04] - **Code, not prompts:** a code step works out every date from the call's `now` value. That covers the callback window, the deadline, the list of allowed promise dates, "this/next <weekday>" and the end-of-week offer. It also works out the product wording and the lowest amount the agent may record.
[11:04] - **Persuasion attempts:** the graph counts them, not the model. Each refusal moves the call one step forward, so an early-band customer gets 1 attempt and a late-band customer gets 2.
[11:04] - **Endings fixed by tool results:**
[11:04]   - Any recorded promise closes the call as `promise`, unless a transfer follows it.
[11:04]   - Running out of wrong identity answers closes it as `not_verified` / `failed`.
[11:04]   - A second failed `create_promise` closes it as `no_promise` / `service_error`.
[11:04] 
[11:04] **Choices the brief does not cover:**
[11:04] - If the account lookup or a transfer fails, the call closes as `no_promise` / `service_error`.
[11:04] - A callback can be booked for today even when today is not a business day. I read "today or the next business day" literally.
[11:04] 
[11:04] **Gaps:**
[11:04] - Asking for a human is handled from the identity step onward. In the opening step, before the person has confirmed who they are, it is not handled.
[11:04] - If several products are late and the customer mentions hardship, the agent picks the product for any promise itself. This only matters when there is more than one late product.
